# NOTE: This is a conceptual placeholder. Actual Taproot scripts require:
# - Proper Schnorr signature handling
# - Taproot tree construction
# - Witness version 1 encoding

# Conceptual structure for a staking/slashing contract:

# Key Path Spending (normal unstaking):
# - Schnorr signature from staker
# - Timelock condition (minimum stake duration)

# Script Path 1: Slashing (violation detected)
# - Oracle signature (from ALYGN Slashing Engine)
# - Proof of violation (hash commitment)
# - Burns tokens or redistributes to validators

# Script Path 2: Emergency Exit
# - Multi-sig from Sovereign Circle
# - Used for critical system issues

# Pseudo-script (not valid Bitcoin Script):
#
# OP_IF
#   # Slashing path
#   <oracle_pubkey> OP_CHECKSIGVERIFY
#   <violation_hash> OP_EQUALVERIFY
#   OP_TRUE
# OP_ELSE
#   OP_IF
#     # Normal unstake path
#     <staker_pubkey> OP_CHECKSIGVERIFY
#     <locktime> OP_CHECKLOCKTIMEVERIFY OP_DROP
#     OP_TRUE
#   OP_ELSE
#     # Emergency path
#     <2> <sovereign_key_1> <sovereign_key_2> <sovereign_key_3> <3> OP_CHECKMULTISIG
#   OP_ENDIF
# OP_ENDIF
